# netsurf: grid track var() from other sheets; restore the keyword-track fallback (patch 340)
# Generated 2026-10-30
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 339)
#
#  - Cross-sheet var(). Patch 336 expands a var() in grid-template-columns
#    from the same sheet only. MDN defines --layout-* in styles-global.css
#    and lays out the page in a chunk sheet, so its page grid still fell
#    back to one column. Every sheet the main rewrite sees now registers
#    its top-level, non-print `--name: value` definitions in a bounded
#    process-wide table (384 entries, value < 256 bytes, last definition
#    wins), and a name not defined in the sheet itself is looked up there.
#    It depends on order: a definition from a sheet converted later (or
#    from a previous page) is what it is. It only serves this text-level
#    grid compile, where the alternative is a single column.
#  - A var() the rewrite still cannot expand (the defining sheet was not
#    converted yet, so sheet order no longer matters) is kept: the
#    declaration becomes `-macsurf-grid: var(...)` and libcss substitutes
#    it at cascade time. 340-libcss lets -macsurf-grid parse the raw
#    track list it then receives (line names, minmax(), repeat(), rem).
#  - Fix in 336's emitter (macsurf__emit_one_track). 336 deleted the
#    fallback that turns a non-value token into one 1fr track, so
#    min-content / max-content / fit-content and other keyword tracks
#    went to -macsurf-grid verbatim, and that parser ENDS the track list
#    at an unknown ident (`max-content 1fr` became one column). Restored.
#    The same hunk pointed tok_to_emit at a buffer declared in an inner
#    block and read it after the block ended (undefined behaviour). The
#    buffer now has function scope.
#
# Gate: CSS-grid-var-crosssheet (GRIDXSHEET340 4/4, Chromium 4/4): `max-content
# 1fr` and `min-content 100px 1fr` keep their tracks (0/2 after 336), and
# a var() defined in another <style> sheet resolves (200 / 32 gap /
# 368). Without this patch it reads 0/4.
